---
description: Traceway writes go through the command bus. Reads use query-builder queries.
globs: app/**/*.php,routes/**/*.php,tests/**/*.php
alwaysApply: false
---

Before changing a save, update, delete, export, or a screen that reads account or route data, read `.agents/skills/traceway-cqrs/SKILL.md`.

Dispatch one readonly command for a write. Read screens with `DB::table` in `App\Queries`. Do not call `Model::create()`, `update()`, or `delete()` from a controller for a fact that already has a command. Do not load `SavedRoute` to render a page. Do not store a password or a two-factor secret anywhere except the user columns Fortify already uses.

`phparkitect.php` is the layer check. `vendor/bin/phparkitect check` must pass. Add a rule there when a new boundary should hold.
